{
  "level": "Year 7",
  "subject": "selective",
  "title": "Editing and proofreading",
  "frames": [
    {
      "heading": "Editing vs proofreading",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Fast writers make small slips. A missing full stop, their instead of there."
        },
        {
          "say": "Editing is improving. A better word, a clearer sentence.",
          "write": "Editing = improving"
        },
        {
          "say": "Proofreading is correcting. Spelling, punctuation and grammar.",
          "write": "Proofreading = correcting"
        },
        {
          "say": "Edit while you write. Save the last minutes for proofreading.",
          "write": "edit as you go, proofread last"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The three-minute routine",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "Here is a routine for the last three minutes.",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
            "alt": "Three-minute checking routine",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 520,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "blue",
                "label": "1. Read for sense (1 min)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 120,
                "w": 520,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "2. Hunt your top errors (1.5 min)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 200,
                "w": 520,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "3. Check the edges (30 s)"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "First, read quickly for sense. Are words missing or repeated?",
          "write": "1: read for sense"
        },
        {
          "say": "Then hunt your top errors. Especially the ones you usually make.",
          "write": "2: hunt top errors",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 280,
            "alt": "Step 2 highlighted",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 40,
                "w": 520,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "grey",
                "label": "1. Read for sense (1 min)"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 120,
                "w": 520,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "orange",
                "label": "2. Hunt your top errors (1.5 min)",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 200,
                "w": 520,
                "h": 60,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "3. Check the edges (30 s)"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Last, check the edges. A capital at the start, a full stop at the end.",
          "write": "3: Capital ... full stop."
        },
        {
          "say": "Fix things neatly. Do not rewrite whole paragraphs at the end."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Comma splices and fragments",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The match was cancelled, it had rained all night. Is that right?",
          "write": "✗ cancelled, it had rained"
        },
        {
          "say": "Both sides of the comma are full sentences. A comma alone is not enough.",
          "write": "two sentences + comma = ✗"
        },
        {
          "say": "Swap the comma for because. Now the link is clear.",
          "write": "cancelled because it had rained",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 140,
            "alt": "The comma replaced with because",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 80,
                "text": "The match was cancelled",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 250,
                "y": 30,
                "w": 121,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": ",",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 250,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 121,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "because",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 381,
                "y": 80,
                "text": " it had rained.",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Just deleting the comma makes a run-on. Still wrong.",
          "write": "✗ cancelled it had rained"
        },
        {
          "say": "Because the bus was late, on its own, is a fragment. Add a main clause.",
          "write": "We missed assembly because..."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Agreement and tense",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The box of old photos are under the bed. Find the subject.",
          "write": "The box of old photos are..."
        },
        {
          "say": "Cover the middle words. The box is. One box, so is.",
          "write": "The box ... is",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 150,
            "alt": "Middle words covered, verb fixed",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 90,
                "text": "The box",
                "size": 24,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start",
                "bold": true
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 120,
                "y": 62,
                "w": 200,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "grey",
                "label": "of old photos",
                "change": "highlight"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 320,
                "y": 32,
                "w": 70,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "are",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 320,
                "y": 92,
                "w": 70,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "is",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 400,
                "y": 90,
                "text": "under the bed.",
                "size": 20,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "We walked to the beach and we see a seal. The tense slips.",
          "write": "✗ walked ... see"
        },
        {
          "say": "Keep it in the past. We walked, and we saw a seal.",
          "write": "✓ walked ... saw",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 140,
            "alt": "Tense slip fixed from see to saw",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 80,
                "text": "We walked and we",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 180,
                "y": 30,
                "w": 69,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "see",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 180,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 69,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "saw",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 259,
                "y": 80,
                "text": " a seal.",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Apostrophes and sound-alikes",
      "lines": [
        {
          "say": "The dog wagged it's tail. Expand it. The dog wagged it is tail? Nonsense.",
          "write": "✗ it's tail = it is tail"
        },
        {
          "say": "Its with no apostrophe means belonging to it. Like his and hers.",
          "write": "✓ its tail",
          "draw": {
            "type": "shapes",
            "width": 560,
            "height": 140,
            "alt": "it's replaced by its",
            "items": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 20,
                "y": 80,
                "text": "The dog wagged",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 160,
                "y": 30,
                "w": 82,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "white",
                "label": "it's",
                "change": "remove"
              },
              {
                "kind": "rect",
                "x": 160,
                "y": 90,
                "w": 82,
                "h": 40,
                "fill": "green",
                "label": "its",
                "change": "add"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "x": 252,
                "y": 80,
                "text": " tail.",
                "size": 18,
                "color": "black",
                "anchor": "start"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "say": "Plain plurals never take an apostrophe. Bananas for sale.",
          "write": "✗ banana's for sale"
        },
        {
          "say": "There is a place. Their means belonging to them. They're means they are.",
          "write": "there · their · they're"
        },
        {
          "say": "Could have, never could of. It only sounds like of.",
          "write": "could have ✓  could of ✗"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
